            <ArticleTitle>Vertical cleft through the superior articular process of the lumbar spine: fracture or anomaly? Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>406-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is reported in which roentgenograms of the lumbar spine showed a vertical cleft in the superior articular process of the L-5 vertebra. The cleft seemed to be of no clinical significance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
